# Go modules (T-P5-GO): the go command downloads and builds a tiny module with two small public dependencies through
# a proxy of proxy.golang.org (checksums verified against sum.golang.org through the repository's sumdb/ proxy), then
# again through a group (tests/clients/README.md; Documents/Operations/clients/go.md).

# The module proxy and the checksum database (the server fetches both; the go command reaches neither directly).
HOSTS="proxy.golang.org sum.golang.org"
# golang:1.25-trixie (go, curl).
CLIENT=go
NEEDS_STACK=1
# Two small modules without dependencies (github.com/google/uuid, github.com/Masterminds/semver/v3): their lists,
# .info, .mod and .zip files, the checksum database lookups and the tiles that prove them.
FIXTURE_BUDGET_KB=1024
